  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Isometric Build\n\nAn isometric tile grid springs up row by row into a stepped block sculpture with one accent tower, then holds.\n\nCategory: motion-graphics. Length: 3 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- An opener or section break should build something in about a second, a small city or stack that reads as infrastructure, platform or growth.\n- A product story about building, scaling or assembling needs a flat, monochrome isometric visual with one highlighted piece.\n- A beat should end on a still, composed object that can hold under a title or a caption.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The stack should come apart to explain layers, with labels: use exploded-view.\n- The blocks should rebuild a logo or pixel art: use brick-mosaic.\n- The build should be flat 2D shapes rather than isometric volume: use bauhaus-build.\n\nVariables:\n- grid (number, 2-9): Tiles per side, default 5\n- max_height (number, 0.5-4): Max height, default 2.2\n- stagger (number, 0-6): Stagger, default 2\n- gap (number, 0-0.3): Gap, default 0.04\n- floors (boolean): Floor lines, default true\n- seed (number, 1-50): Seed, default 4\n- speed (number, 0.1-4): Speed, default 1\n- background (color): Background, default \"#111111\"\n- color (color): Blocks, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- accent (color): Accent tower, default \"#E5322D\"\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Isometric Build\n\n  An isometric tile grid springs up row by row into a stepped block sculpture with one accent tower, then holds.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/isometric-build/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"isometric-build\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"grid\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Tiles per side\", \"description\": \"Tiles along each side of the square grid.\", \"default\": 5, \"min\": 2, \"max\": 9, \"step\": 1},\n    {\"id\": \"max_height\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Max height\", \"description\": \"Tallest regular block, in tile widths. The accent tower rises above it.\", \"default\": 2.2, \"min\": 0.5, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.1},\n    {\"id\": \"stagger\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Stagger\", \"description\": \"Frames between consecutive diagonals rising.\", \"default\": 2, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 6, \"step\": 0.5, \"unit\": \"frames\"},\n    {\"id\": \"gap\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Gap\", \"description\": \"Gap between neighbouring blocks, as a share of a tile.\", \"default\": 0.04, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 0.3, \"step\": 0.01},\n    {\"id\": \"floors\", \"type\": \"boolean\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Floor lines\", \"description\": \"Draw floor lines on the block faces.\", \"default\": true},\n    {\"id\": \"seed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Seed\", \"description\": \"Changes the block heights and which tower is the accent.\", \"default\": 4, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 50, \"step\": 1},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed of the build.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.1, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.1},\n    {\"id\": \"background\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Background\", \"description\": \"Background color.\", \"default\": \"#111111\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Blocks\", \"description\": \"Block color; side faces are this color shaded toward the background.\", \"default\": \"#FFFFFF\"},\n    {\"id\": \"accent\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Accent tower\", \"description\": \"Color of the single accent tower.\", \"default\": \"#E5322D\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Isometric Build</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        #root { background: #111111; }\n        .ib-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; }\n        .ib-stage svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"isometric-build\" data-duration=\"3\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"ib-clip\" class=\"ib-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <svg id=\"ib-svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Isometric city build\"></svg>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              if (typeof value === \"boolean\") return value;\n              if (value === \"true\") return true;\n              if (value === \"false\") return false;\n              return fallback;\n            }\n            var FPS = 30;\n            var W = root.clientWidth || 1080;\n            var H = root.clientHeight || 1920;\n\n            // Seeded random in [0, 1): a string hash, so the same key always gives the same value.\n            function rnd(key) {\n              var h = 1779033703 ^ key.length;\n              for (var i = 0; i < key.length; i++) {\n                h = Math.imul(h ^ key.charCodeAt(i), 3432918353);\n                h = (h << 13) | (h >>> 19);\n              }\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 16), 2246822507);\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 3266489909);\n              h ^= h >>> 16;\n              return (h >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n            }\n\n            // Piecewise-linear map of x from inR to outR, optionally eased per segment and clamped.\n            function interp(x, inR, outR, o) {\n              o = o || {};\n              var n = inR.length;\n              var i = 0;\n              if (x >= inR[n - 1]) i = n - 2;\n              else if (x > inR[0]) { while (x > inR[i + 1]) i++; }\n              var t = (x - inR[i]) / (inR[i + 1] - inR[i]);\n              if (o.clamp !== false) t = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, t));\n              if (o.easing) t = o.easing(t);\n              return outR[i] + (outR[i + 1] - outR[i]) * t;\n            }\n            function clamp01(t) { return Math.min(1, Math.max(0, t)); }\n\n            // Closed-form damped spring from 0 to 1 (rest at 1), sampled at `frame` frames.\n            function spring(frame, mass, stiffness, damping) {\n              if (frame <= 0) return 0;\n              var t = frame / FPS;\n              var w0 = Math.sqrt(stiffness / mass);\n              var z = damping / (2 * Math.sqrt(stiffness * mass));\n              if (z < 1) {\n                var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n                return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + ((z * w0) / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n              }\n              return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n            }\n\n            function fmt(n) { return Math.round(n * 10) / 10; }\n\n            var SVGNS = \"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\";\n            function el(tag, attrs, parent) {\n              var e = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, tag);\n              for (var k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]);\n              if (parent) parent.appendChild(e);\n              return e;\n            }\n\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            // Runs draw(frame) from the timeline so seeking to a time always draws the same picture.\n            function drive(frames, draw) {\n              var clock = { frame: 0 };\n              tl.to(clock, { frame: frames, duration: frames / FPS, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.frame); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n            }\n\n            var grid = Math.round(num(vars.grid, 5, 2, 9));\n            var maxHeight = num(vars.max_height, 2.2, 0.5, 4);\n            var stagger = num(vars.stagger, 2, 0, 6);\n            var gap = num(vars.gap, 0.04, 0, 0.3);\n            var floors = bool(vars.floors, true);\n            var seed = Math.round(num(vars.seed, 4, 1, 50));\n            var speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.1, 4);\n            var background = str(vars.background, \"#111111\");\n            root.style.background = background;\n            var color = str(vars.color, \"#FFFFFF\");\n            var accent = str(vars.accent, \"#E5322D\");\n\n            var ISO_Y = Math.tan(Math.PI / 6), ISO_Z = 1 / Math.cos(Math.PI / 6);\n            var FLOOR = 0.42, SHADE_LEFT = 0.32, SHADE_RIGHT = 0.6;\n            var n = grid, inset = Math.min(0.45, Math.max(0, gap)) / 2;\n            function r(key) { return rnd(\"isometric-build-\" + seed + \"-\" + key); }\n\n            // Blocks in painter order (back to front); front rows rise first.\n            var inner = Math.max(1, n - 2);\n            var ai = n > 2 ? 1 + Math.floor(r(\"ai\") * inner) : 0;\n            var aj = n > 2 ? 1 + Math.floor(r(\"aj\") * inner) : 0;\n            var blocks = [];\n            for (var sum = 0; sum <= 2 * (n - 1); sum++) {\n              for (var i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                var j = sum - i;\n                if (j < 0 || j >= n) continue;\n                var isAccent = i === ai && j === aj;\n                // One compact mound that peaks in the middle, snapped to whole floors.\n                var c = (n - 1) / 2;\n                var centre = 1 - Math.hypot(i - c, j - c) / (Math.hypot(c, c) || 1);\n                var raw = maxHeight * (0.2 + 0.8 * Math.pow(centre, 1.3)) * (0.75 + 0.5 * r(\"h\" + i + \"-\" + j));\n                var h = Math.max(FLOOR, Math.round(raw / FLOOR) * FLOOR);\n                blocks.push({ i: i, j: j, accent: isAccent, height: isAccent ? maxHeight * 1.35 : h,\n                  delay: (2 * (n - 1) - sum) * stagger + r(\"d\" + i + \"-\" + j) * stagger });\n              }\n            }\n\n            var tallest = maxHeight * 1.35;\n            var a = Math.min((W * 0.64) / (2 * n), (H * 0.8) / (2 * n * ISO_Y + tallest * ISO_Z));\n            var b = a * ISO_Y, hz = a * ISO_Z;\n            var top = (H - (2 * n * b + tallest * hz)) / 2 + tallest * hz;\n            var cx = W / 2;\n            function P(u, v, z) { return fmt(cx + (u - v) * a) + \" \" + fmt(top + (u + v) * b - z * hz); }\n            function poly() { return \"M \" + Array.prototype.slice.call(arguments).join(\" L \") + \" Z\"; }\n            var unit = Math.min(W, H) / 720;\n\n            var svg = document.getElementById(\"ib-svg\");\n            svg.setAttribute(\"viewBox\", \"0 0 \" + W + \" \" + H);\n            var ground = \"\";\n            for (var k = 0; k <= n; k++) ground += \"M \" + P(k, 0, 0) + \" L \" + P(k, n, 0) + \" M \" + P(0, k, 0) + \" L \" + P(n, k, 0) + \" \";\n            el(\"path\", { d: ground, fill: \"none\", stroke: color, \"stroke-opacity\": 0.12, \"stroke-width\": unit }, svg);\n\n            blocks.forEach(function (blk) {\n              var fill = blk.accent ? accent : color;\n              var g = el(\"g\", { opacity: 0 }, svg);\n              blk.g = g;\n              blk.left = el(\"path\", { fill: fill }, g);\n              el(\"path\", { fill: background, \"fill-opacity\": SHADE_LEFT }, g); blk.leftShade = g.lastChild;\n              blk.right = el(\"path\", { fill: fill }, g);\n              el(\"path\", { fill: background, \"fill-opacity\": SHADE_RIGHT }, g); blk.rightShade = g.lastChild;\n              blk.lines = el(\"path\", { fill: \"none\", stroke: background, \"stroke-opacity\": 0.35, \"stroke-width\": unit * 1.2 }, g);\n              blk.roof = el(\"path\", { fill: fill, stroke: background, \"stroke-opacity\": 0.5, \"stroke-width\": unit, \"stroke-linejoin\": \"round\" }, g);\n            });\n\n            function draw(frame) {\n              var time = frame * speed;\n              blocks.forEach(function (blk) {\n                var s = spring(time - blk.delay, 0.7, 140, 11);\n                var opacity = interp(s, [0, 0.15], [0, 1]);\n                if (opacity <= 0) { blk.g.setAttribute(\"opacity\", 0); return; }\n                var h = Math.max(0.02, blk.height * s);\n                var u0 = blk.i + inset, u1 = blk.i + 1 - inset, v0 = blk.j + inset, v1 = blk.j + 1 - inset;\n                var left = poly(P(u0, v1, 0), P(u1, v1, 0), P(u1, v1, h), P(u0, v1, h));\n                var right = poly(P(u1, v0, 0), P(u1, v1, 0), P(u1, v1, h), P(u1, v0, h));\n                var roof = poly(P(u0, v0, h), P(u1, v0, h), P(u1, v1, h), P(u0, v1, h));\n                var lines = \"\";\n                if (floors) for (var z = FLOOR; z < h - FLOOR * 0.5; z += FLOOR) lines += \"M \" + P(u0, v1, z) + \" L \" + P(u1, v1, z) + \" L \" + P(u1, v0, z) + \" \";\n                blk.g.setAttribute(\"opacity\", opacity);\n                blk.left.setAttribute(\"d\", left); blk.leftShade.setAttribute(\"d\", left);\n                blk.right.setAttribute(\"d\", right); blk.rightShade.setAttribute(\"d\", right);\n                blk.lines.setAttribute(\"d\", lines);\n                blk.roof.setAttribute(\"d\", roof);\n              });\n            }\n            drive(Math.round(parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3\") * FPS), draw);\n\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3\");\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"isometric-build\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
